{"pageProps":{"data":{"city":"Houston","state_abbr":"TX","project_name":"Kitchen Remodel","city_slug":"houston-tx","project_slug":"kitchen-remodel","project_size":200,"project_unit":"SF","regional_premium_percentage":-5,"calculated_costs":{"low":30182,"median":80484,"high":160968},"breakdown":{"labor_estimate":32194,"material_estimate":48290},"local_wage":null,"trade":null,"watch_outs":["Foundation Movement & Expansive Clay: Texas has some of the worst expansive soil conditions in the US, causing widespread foundation issues Clay soil expands when wet and shrinks when dry, cracking foundations. Reddit users insist on foundation evaluation before any major remodel. Maintaining consistent soil moisture (soaker hoses around foundation) helps prevent movement. Many homes need pier work eventually.","No State Contractor License: Texas has no statewide general contractor licensing—verification falls on the homeowner Unlike California, Texas doesn","Extreme Heat & HVAC Sizing: Texas summers push HVAC systems to their limits—proper sizing is critical Oversized or undersized AC units are common complaints. Reddit users insist on Manual J load calculations, not just \"one ton per 500 sq ft\" rules of thumb. Variable-speed systems handle Texas heat better. Also verify SEER ratings meet current standards.","Hail Damage & Roofing: Texas leads the nation in hail claims—roofing is a major concern Hail storms bring out roofing scammers in force. Reddit warns about \"free inspections\" that find damage, insurance assignment scams, and contractors who disappear after collecting the insurance check. Stick with established local companies.","Hurricane & Wind Ratings (Coastal): Texas Gulf Coast has strict wind-load requirements that increase project costs Coastal counties require wind-rated materials, hurricane straps, and impact-resistant glazing in many cases. Reddit users report 15-25% higher costs on the coast versus inland. Verify your wind zone before accepting bids."],"data_sourc